INSERT IGNORE INTO `qlo_rural_activity_lang` VALUES
(1,1,'Morning milking & butter churning','Farm experience','2 hours','All year','Join the dairy at dawn - milk the cows, churn butter and carry it to the breakfast table.','The cows are milked at first light, and guests can join in before the farm settles into its day. Churning the butter by hand takes longer and tastes better than anything from a shop, and in the kitchen it becomes the day\'s ghee.'),
(2,1,'Field-to-table cooking','Farm experience','Half day','Oct - Mar','Harvest what is in season - greens, millet, citrus - then cook it on a clay stove with the family.','Walk the field with the family, pick what is ready, and cook it the way it has been cooked here for generations - over a clay stove, in iron, with time. Lunch is what you made.'),
(3,1,'Fishpond afternoon','Farm experience','1 hour','All year','The farm\'s rearing pond supplies the table - learn how it works and try your hand at the catch.','The pond on the farm\'s edge is a working fishery. Feed the fish, learn about the pond\'s cycle with the fisherman, and if you are lucky the evening\'s meal is your catch.'),
(4,1,'Sarus crane birdwalk','Outdoors','2 hours','Nov - Feb','Walk the village wetlands at dusk - sarus cranes, egrets and the winter migrants are regulars.','Northern India\'s wetlands hold some of the finest bird life on the subcontinent. At dusk the fields fill with sarus cranes - carry binoculars and walk quietly.'),
(5,1,'Village walk & crafts','Outdoors','2 hours','All year','Meet the potters, weavers and beekeepers of the neighbouring hamlets, guided by the property.','The lanes around the farm are full of crafts - potters at their wheels, weavers at the loom, and homesteads making pickles and honey. Your host knows every family and every story.'),
(6,1,'Orchard & crop tour','Farm experience','3 hours','Oct - Mar','A guided walk through the farm\'s orchards and fields - what grows here, and how it reaches the market.','From mango and guava orchards to the mustard and millet rotations, the tour follows the farm year - what is planted, what is harvested, and where the produce goes. Questions welcome.');
